00:34:22.510 --> 00:34:22.990
It's Jan.

764
00:34:24.270 --> 00:34:30.270
And uh-oh, Jan is calling to tell Michael, Michael, I would love to come to casino night.

765
00:34:30.530 --> 00:34:37.570
I feel like you can watch Steve as Michael, like, literally break into a sweat.

766
00:34:38.530 --> 00:34:40.970
He's like, holy crap.

767
00:34:40.970 --> 00:34:49.290
When in a million years did I think that I'd have two women on the line who'd both just said yes to me within seconds of each other?

768
00:34:49.410 --> 00:34:50.750
Two queens on casino night.

769
00:34:50.850 --> 00:34:52.250
Gonna have to drop a deuce.

770
00:34:52.770 --> 00:34:53.730
Oh, boy.

771
00:34:54.050 --> 00:34:56.230
So that's a big cliffhanger.

772
00:34:56.410 --> 00:34:59.410
We go into, like, what would normally be a commercial break right there.

773
00:34:59.790 --> 00:35:00.950
Should we go into a break?

774
00:35:01.110 --> 00:35:04.490
Let's go into a break because now we're going to get into the casino game.

775
00:35:04.890 --> 00:35:07.850
And a lot, a lot is going to happen.

776
00:35:07.850 --> 00:35:14.680
All right, we are back and we are at the casino.

777
00:35:15.200 --> 00:35:16.400
The casino is open.

778
00:35:16.740 --> 00:35:17.800
Gambling is happening.

779
00:35:18.140 --> 00:35:19.340
It's open for business.

780
00:35:20.040 --> 00:35:22.100
At 13 minutes, 22 seconds.

781
00:35:22.720 --> 00:35:24.320
It is happening, Jenna.

782
00:35:24.580 --> 00:35:26.460
You are wearing quite the dress.

783
00:35:26.800 --> 00:35:29.020
Oh, actually, everyone got very dressed up for this.

784
00:35:29.200 --> 00:35:31.100
We got a ton of mail about your dress.

785
00:35:31.400 --> 00:35:36.400
Matt Mabe said, how many different dresses did you try on before you settled on the blue one that you wore?

786
00:35:36.400 --> 00:35:43.560
Danny Thurgood said, my wife has a theory that the dress Pam wears was an old bridesmaid's dress that Pam had in her closet.

787
00:35:44.740 --> 00:35:49.580
Danny, I wrote on a note card, Pam in a bridesmaid's dress, question mark.

788
00:35:49.980 --> 00:35:52.340
It really looks like a bridesmaid's dress.

789
00:35:52.520 --> 00:35:53.360
It really does.

790
00:35:53.640 --> 00:35:53.860
Yes.

791
00:35:53.860 --> 00:36:01.040
And then, original Gus girl said, whose decision was it for Pam to wear her watch with her gown?

792
00:36:01.040 --> 00:36:04.240
It was a subtle but great costuming and character choice.

793
00:36:04.480 --> 00:36:06.640
I love all of these questions.

794
00:36:07.360 --> 00:36:09.460
You guys are so observant.

795
00:36:09.840 --> 00:36:10.560
All right.

796
00:36:10.760 --> 00:36:16.440
Let me start by saying, Angela and Danny's wife, you guys are correct.

797
00:36:17.020 --> 00:36:18.220
Was it a bridesmaid's dress?

798
00:36:18.220 --> 00:36:20.640
Well, that was the inspiration.

799
00:36:20.740 --> 00:36:27.780
When I met with Carrie, our wardrobe designer, about this outfit that Pam would wear, we said,

800
00:36:28.140 --> 00:36:29.380
you know what?

801
00:36:29.380 --> 00:36:32.320
We want her to be dressed up in like a cocktail dress.

802
00:36:32.320 --> 00:36:38.800
But on Pam's salary and just thinking about Pam's life, when would she ever buy a cocktail dress?

803
00:36:38.980 --> 00:36:42.220
And she's certainly not going to buy one just for casino night.

804
00:36:42.220 --> 00:36:46.060
So we had a whole conversation where we were like, you know what?

805
00:36:46.620 --> 00:36:50.680
I think she re-wears an old bridesmaid's dress.

806
00:36:50.920 --> 00:36:53.080
That's the fanciest thing she has in her closet.

807
00:36:53.080 --> 00:36:54.220
And that's what she wears.

808
00:36:54.480 --> 00:36:58.160
I'll have you know, that was the first dress I tried on.

809
00:36:58.780 --> 00:37:00.040
We loved it.

810
00:37:00.140 --> 00:37:02.660
She had a whole rack of dresses and I tried them all on.

811
00:37:02.760 --> 00:37:03.520
That was our favorite.

812
00:37:04.060 --> 00:37:07.660
And we sent that picture to Greg and he approved it immediately.

813
00:37:08.020 --> 00:37:10.080
It was like a winner from the start.

814
00:37:10.080 --> 00:37:15.740
Well, that is so great and perfect and really answers my burning question.

815
00:37:15.820 --> 00:37:19.920
Because I was like, I feel like I wore a bridesmaid's dress that looks similar to that.

816
00:37:20.120 --> 00:37:20.320
Yeah.

817
00:37:20.820 --> 00:37:22.440
To a wedding in the 90s.

818
00:37:22.520 --> 00:37:26.940
By the way, I love that watch question, Angela, because that was a discussion.

819
00:37:27.480 --> 00:37:30.780
It was a discussion that Pam wears that watch every day.

820
00:37:30.920 --> 00:37:32.200
Most of the time you can't see it.

821
00:37:32.300 --> 00:37:35.760
But every day, Phil Shea would come up to me and he had a little tray.

822
00:37:35.760 --> 00:37:41.560
And it had my watch and it had my Pam wedding ring on it or my Pam engagement ring on it.

823
00:37:41.840 --> 00:37:46.080
And you pick it up, you put it on first thing in the morning, take it off at the end of the night.

824
00:37:46.240 --> 00:37:50.440
And so I've always been wearing that watch, but you cannot normally see it because it's

825
00:37:50.440 --> 00:37:51.680
underneath my sleeve, right?

826
00:37:52.220 --> 00:37:53.680
So we had a whole discussion.

827
00:37:53.880 --> 00:37:57.420
Does Pam wear her watch with her fancy dress or not?

828
00:37:57.420 --> 00:38:01.880
And we thought, listen, guys, this is back before iPhones.

829
00:38:02.200 --> 00:38:06.440
You didn't have the time in your back pocket the way you do now.

830
00:38:06.640 --> 00:38:10.200
And we discussed that Pam does not have a fancy watch.

831
00:38:10.680 --> 00:38:13.820
So she's got one watch and she wore it.

832
00:38:13.940 --> 00:38:16.120
And I can't believe someone noticed that detail.

833
00:38:16.600 --> 00:38:17.620
Thanks for noticing.

834
00:38:17.920 --> 00:38:19.120
Pam would wear her watch.

835
00:38:19.240 --> 00:38:20.520
That made such sense to me.

836
00:38:20.660 --> 00:38:21.200
I love it.

837
00:38:21.320 --> 00:38:24.460
I feel like she also probably has a pair of Keds on standby.

838
00:38:24.460 --> 00:38:27.020
That she could change into.

839
00:38:27.380 --> 00:38:28.160
I love that.

840
00:38:28.360 --> 00:38:30.360
Angela, what about your dress?

841
00:38:30.580 --> 00:38:34.100
You're wearing a black dress, which is in your color scheme.

842
00:38:34.240 --> 00:38:39.140
But I mean, it's a little bit, it's a bit, what?

843
00:38:39.320 --> 00:38:39.840
Sultry.

844
00:38:40.000 --> 00:38:40.800
It's somewhat tight.

845
00:38:41.320 --> 00:38:43.280
It's an LBD for sure.

846
00:38:43.280 --> 00:38:45.280
It is a little black dress.

847
00:38:45.660 --> 00:38:48.120
I mean, I have a little bit of cleavage.

848
00:38:48.360 --> 00:38:48.580
Yeah.

849
00:38:48.680 --> 00:38:49.120
A little bit.

850
00:38:49.340 --> 00:38:50.100
A little bit.

851
00:38:50.220 --> 00:38:52.100
It is a tight little black dress.

852
00:38:52.100 --> 00:38:58.260
I feel like she probably wore it to a funeral and maybe it had some lace attachment over

853
00:38:58.260 --> 00:39:04.140
her decotage, but maybe she's feeling a little, a little saucy.

854
00:39:04.280 --> 00:39:07.080
So she was like, I'm not going to wear this sweater that goes with it.

855
00:39:07.200 --> 00:39:10.300
I do have a sweater that comes in and out of scenes.

856
00:39:10.440 --> 00:39:13.940
I don't know if you notice at right at the top, I'm holding it.

857
00:39:14.100 --> 00:39:16.160
And then later on you see me wearing it.

858
00:39:16.460 --> 00:39:19.820
But yeah, I know I'm wearing a little black dress.

859
00:39:19.820 --> 00:39:25.060
So I have to point out, it's jumping around, but I have a great catch of someone breaking

860
00:39:25.060 --> 00:39:25.660
character.

861
00:39:25.860 --> 00:39:26.140
Oh!

862
00:39:26.620 --> 00:39:28.080
And that someone is me.

863
00:39:29.020 --> 00:39:35.280
At 13 minutes, 24 seconds, there's a shot of Angela Martin talking to Meredith.

864
00:39:35.720 --> 00:39:40.020
And you see at the very beginning of the moment, maybe I'm aware that camera's panning over

865
00:39:40.020 --> 00:39:41.260
and so I have a solemn look.

866
00:39:41.260 --> 00:39:46.920
And then clearly I think camera has gone off of us and then I just go, I just like start

867
00:39:46.920 --> 00:39:51.520
gesturing and I think I can make out the words, I have to pee or something.

868
00:39:51.780 --> 00:39:52.640
Oh my gosh!

869
00:39:52.640 --> 00:39:53.780
What else is going on?

870
00:39:53.840 --> 00:39:55.420
Are you in the background of another scene?

871
00:39:55.440 --> 00:39:59.640
I'm in the background of an establishing shot of you and Roy gambling.

872
00:40:00.100 --> 00:40:02.260
And then it pans over to the rest of us.

873
00:40:02.400 --> 00:40:03.420
Jim's at another table.

874
00:40:03.420 --> 00:40:04.640
I'm talking to Meredith.

875
00:40:04.760 --> 00:40:05.960
I'm holding my sweater.

876
00:40:05.960 --> 00:40:09.620
And at the very beginning of it, I have a solemn face.

877
00:40:09.760 --> 00:40:11.880
And then within seconds, I think the camera's gone.

878
00:40:12.060 --> 00:40:13.140
I just start being chatty.

879
00:40:13.280 --> 00:40:15.500
It's 100% me just talking.

880
00:40:15.740 --> 00:40:16.340
Oh my gosh!

881
00:40:17.240 --> 00:40:18.820
All right, should we get into it now?

882
00:40:18.860 --> 00:40:19.740
Let's get into it.

883
00:40:19.900 --> 00:40:21.360
Creed is stealing poker chips.

884
00:40:21.520 --> 00:40:22.480
Carol has arrived.

885
00:40:22.940 --> 00:40:25.100
Dwight is Michael's wingman, I guess.

886
00:40:25.440 --> 00:40:28.840
And Toby just beat Michael at cards.

887
00:40:29.040 --> 00:40:29.520
Yes.

888
00:40:29.660 --> 00:40:32.260
And I have a few fan questions about that stuff.

889
00:40:32.420 --> 00:40:34.660
The first one comes from Jessica Merkner.

890
00:40:34.660 --> 00:40:37.860
She says, Dwight is a terrible wingman.

891
00:40:38.080 --> 00:40:41.840
His inability to warn Michael that Jan is coming is great.

892
00:40:42.180 --> 00:40:44.100
Was any of that improvised?

893
00:40:44.480 --> 00:40:46.020
All right, so I looked at the script.

894
00:40:46.640 --> 00:40:50.560
And you know when Carol first arrives and Dwight comes up and says,

895
00:40:50.980 --> 00:40:52.660
Code REMAX is here.

896
00:40:52.800 --> 00:40:55.740
But no sign of Lan Jevonson.

897
00:40:55.900 --> 00:40:56.400
Yeah.

898
00:40:56.620 --> 00:40:57.260
It's so good.

899
00:40:57.460 --> 00:40:59.660
That second part was improvised.

900
00:41:00.020 --> 00:41:00.980
So I'm not sure.

901
00:41:01.160 --> 00:41:01.210
That's so good.

902
00:41:01.380 --> 00:41:01.860
I know.

903
00:41:01.860 --> 00:41:05.580
I'm not sure if Brain did it or if it was like one of the writer pitches on set,

904
00:41:05.680 --> 00:41:07.840
because we would have writers on set that would pitch us jokes.

905
00:41:08.000 --> 00:41:10.480
But the original line was supposed to be,

906
00:41:10.960 --> 00:41:13.080
No sign of date number two.

907
00:41:14.020 --> 00:41:17.760
Which is also very funny because it is in no way coded.

908
00:41:17.980 --> 00:41:22.140
And also, out loud, he says Michael has a second date.

909
00:41:22.140 --> 00:41:30.180
All right, so Jenna, at 18 minutes, 26 seconds, I have a card called Kiss Slap Smirk.

910
00:41:30.560 --> 00:41:32.220
Oh, this is a classic.

911
00:41:32.500 --> 00:41:34.800
This is a classic Dwight-Angela moment.

912
00:41:35.040 --> 00:41:41.460
It's when Dwight is playing craps and Angela walks up in her little black dress and she's like,

913
00:41:41.520 --> 00:41:42.140
What are you doing?

914
00:41:42.400 --> 00:41:44.480
And they're very formal with one another.

915
00:41:44.660 --> 00:41:44.860
Yeah.

916
00:41:45.040 --> 00:41:45.640
Very formal.

917
00:41:45.640 --> 00:41:47.840
And he's like, Angela, I need to roll an eight.

918
00:41:47.960 --> 00:41:48.700
And everyone wins.

919
00:41:48.800 --> 00:41:50.340
And she says, So roll an eight.

920
00:41:50.700 --> 00:41:52.160
And then he does.

921
00:41:52.440 --> 00:41:52.860
Yes!

922
00:41:53.280 --> 00:41:58.640
And he is so excited that he grabs you and he kisses you on the cheek.

923
00:41:58.940 --> 00:41:59.820
I know.

924
00:41:59.820 --> 00:42:02.760
And listen, even though maybe she's happy about that,

925
00:42:02.940 --> 00:42:06.180
she has to slap him for being inappropriate at work.

926
00:42:06.380 --> 00:42:06.820
Yes.

927
00:42:07.440 --> 00:42:10.840
Well, Angela, we got a fan question from Heather Lindo.

928
00:42:11.300 --> 00:42:12.480
Sam, will you play it?

929
00:42:12.480 --> 00:42:13.180
Hi, Jenna.

930
00:42:13.400 --> 00:42:13.920
Hi, Angela.

931
00:42:14.620 --> 00:42:18.480
Casino Night is one of my very favorite episodes for a lot of reasons.

932
00:42:18.480 --> 00:42:24.600
And one of them being the scene at the craps table when Dwight kisses Angela for good luck

933
00:42:24.600 --> 00:42:25.740
and then she slaps him.

934
00:42:26.000 --> 00:42:29.500
But when she turns around, her face is just perfection.

935
00:42:29.800 --> 00:42:33.000
She cycles through like 10 emotions in a matter of like three seconds.

936
00:42:33.000 --> 00:42:39.520
She is horrified and thrilled and embarrassed and obviously deep down very happy all at the same time.

937
00:42:39.900 --> 00:42:41.060
And I just love it.

938
00:42:41.060 --> 00:42:47.060
And Angela, my question is, did you nail that on the first take or did you have to do it many, many times?

939
00:42:47.280 --> 00:42:49.860
Thank you so much for letting me ask my question.

940
00:42:50.000 --> 00:42:54.660
I know everyone says this, but my sister Kim and I really are the Office number one fans.

941
00:42:54.760 --> 00:42:55.660
We just love you so much.

942
00:42:55.740 --> 00:42:56.220
So thank you.

943
00:42:56.500 --> 00:42:59.140
So sweet.

944
00:42:59.140 --> 00:43:00.760
I love that question so much.

945
00:43:01.620 --> 00:43:02.020
Okay.

946
00:43:02.020 --> 00:43:08.240
So I was very excited about this question because I actually wrote in my journal about the scene.

947
00:43:08.620 --> 00:43:09.560
Of course you did.

948
00:43:09.760 --> 00:43:10.400
Of course we did.

949
00:43:10.520 --> 00:43:12.020
I wrote about it the week we filmed it.

950
00:43:12.220 --> 00:43:17.500
To answer your question, Heather, no, I did not get it right the first time.

951
00:43:17.820 --> 00:43:18.160
Okay.

952
00:43:18.240 --> 00:43:21.540
So I wrote that I was really nervous to slap Rain at firSt.

953
00:43:21.660 --> 00:43:23.280
You know, my slap was kind of timid.

954
00:43:23.280 --> 00:43:27.140
Which makes sense because you were probably very, you were worried about hurting him.

955
00:43:27.640 --> 00:43:28.080
Exactly.

956
00:43:28.080 --> 00:43:29.160
I didn't want to hurt him.

957
00:43:29.300 --> 00:43:30.580
And it wasn't a fake slap.

958
00:43:30.820 --> 00:43:32.200
They told you to really slap him.

959
00:43:32.300 --> 00:43:34.280
That was, they were never did a phony slap.

960
00:43:34.480 --> 00:43:36.000
No, they wanted a real slap.

961
00:43:36.220 --> 00:43:39.260
And well, I guess my timid little slap wasn't working.

962
00:43:39.820 --> 00:43:42.880
So Rain said, listen, Ange, just go for it.

963
00:43:43.020 --> 00:43:44.020
I can take it.

964
00:43:44.240 --> 00:43:47.480
So I started really slapping him.

965
00:43:47.560 --> 00:43:48.240
Oh, no.

966
00:43:48.520 --> 00:43:52.340
And I wrote that it took us about 13 takes to get.

967
00:43:52.380 --> 00:43:52.860
Oh, no.

968
00:43:53.040 --> 00:43:53.420
Yes.

969
00:43:53.980 --> 00:43:56.600
So that's 13 slaps.

970
00:43:56.940 --> 00:43:57.300
All right.

971
00:43:57.500 --> 00:43:59.320
Here's the one thing I need you guys to remember.

972
00:43:59.560 --> 00:44:00.980
I am 5'1".

973
00:44:00.980 --> 00:44:02.520
Rain is like 6'3".

974
00:44:02.520 --> 00:44:06.100
So it wasn't really easy for me to reach his cheek.

975
00:44:06.400 --> 00:44:09.100
And one time my aim was really off.

976
00:44:09.260 --> 00:44:10.420
And I missed his cheek.

977
00:44:10.480 --> 00:44:13.540
And I slapped his ear so hard.

978
00:44:13.880 --> 00:44:15.980
He was like, I'd actually hurt him.

979
00:44:16.080 --> 00:44:17.580
You said there was like a ringing in his ear.

980
00:44:17.780 --> 00:44:19.440
And then the other time I missed.

981
00:44:19.620 --> 00:44:22.040
And I slapped and I hit his glasses.

982
00:44:22.040 --> 00:44:24.600
And I knocked them sideways on his face.

983
00:44:24.840 --> 00:44:25.380
I know.

984
00:44:25.920 --> 00:44:26.700
I know.

985
00:44:27.780 --> 00:44:30.820
Well, I want to go back to something that Heather said, too,

986
00:44:30.940 --> 00:44:34.080
about that look on your face as you're walking away.

987
00:44:34.200 --> 00:44:34.400
Yeah.

988
00:44:34.540 --> 00:44:36.820
Because it is, it is amazing.

989
00:44:37.440 --> 00:44:40.120
And I have the script and I looked it up.

990
00:44:40.200 --> 00:44:46.820
And all it says is that you slapped Dwight and that you smile as you walk away from the table.

991
00:44:47.080 --> 00:44:50.120
I think there's so much more going on in your face.

992
00:44:50.120 --> 00:44:55.080
So your character is angry that Dwight would kiss you so publicly and all of that.

993
00:44:55.220 --> 00:45:00.620
But what I love is that you have this little look to the camera at the very end.

994
00:45:00.620 --> 00:45:03.180
It's like 18 minutes, 48 seconds.

995
00:45:03.520 --> 00:45:04.040
Yeah.

996
00:45:04.260 --> 00:45:08.760
Where you sort of catch the camera catching you smiling.

997
00:45:09.080 --> 00:45:09.180
Right.

998
00:45:09.240 --> 00:45:10.800
That camera catch was not in the script.

999
00:45:10.800 --> 00:45:11.880
Was that improvised?

1000
00:45:12.160 --> 00:45:13.340
Yes, it was.

1001
00:45:13.560 --> 00:45:13.740
Okay.

1002
00:45:13.840 --> 00:45:18.420
So that, that just happened on the day, that little moment where I'm busted at the end.

1003
00:45:18.420 --> 00:45:24.840
And so in one of the early takes, I was walking out of frame and I just looked at camera and I

1004
00:45:24.840 --> 00:45:25.640
quickly looked away.

1005
00:45:25.760 --> 00:45:27.460
Like I was embarrassed that they caught me smiling.

1006
00:45:27.680 --> 00:45:30.460
And our director of photography, Randall Einhorn said,

1007
00:45:30.600 --> 00:45:31.720
Ange, Ange, I caught it.

1008
00:45:31.800 --> 00:45:33.820
I caught it right at the end as you're leaving frame.

1009
00:45:33.820 --> 00:45:36.500
And he really helped me find that moment.

1010
00:45:36.840 --> 00:45:38.240
Then he showed it to our director.

1011
00:45:38.440 --> 00:45:39.420
Our director loved it.

