someone was like, I love how you say Dwight.

1340
00:59:30.330 --> 00:59:31.990
And I was like, how do you say it?

1341
00:59:32.110 --> 00:59:32.770
And they were like, Dwight.

1342
00:59:32.870 --> 00:59:33.990
And I was like, I know, Dwight.

1343
00:59:34.170 --> 00:59:35.270
And they were like, nope, Dwight.

1344
00:59:35.590 --> 00:59:35.730
Dwight.

1345
00:59:35.830 --> 00:59:37.850
And I was like, no, no, I'm saying it right.

1346
00:59:38.050 --> 00:59:38.390
It's Dwight.

1347
00:59:38.530 --> 00:59:39.990
And they were like, nope, it's not.

1348
00:59:39.990 --> 00:59:42.690
So, yes, I auditioned.

1349
00:59:42.890 --> 00:59:46.510
Or no, I was offered to come in and audition for the role of Dwight.

1350
00:59:46.650 --> 00:59:48.070
And I was so excited.

1351
00:59:48.290 --> 00:59:55.350
I had met Allison Jones randomly out in LA on a general meeting when I had zero dollars

1352
00:59:55.350 --> 00:59:55.870
to my name.

1353
00:59:55.970 --> 00:59:59.250
And she said, something's coming on our first meeting, our only meeting.

1354
00:59:59.350 --> 01:00:00.530
She said, something's coming called The Office.

1355
01:00:00.550 --> 01:00:01.210
You'd be great for it.

1356
01:00:01.270 --> 01:00:01.550
I said, great.

1357
01:00:01.890 --> 01:00:03.170
So, then I got back to New York.

1358
01:00:03.970 --> 01:00:07.450
And they said, there's this show called The Office.

1359
01:00:07.510 --> 01:00:10.810
And I was like, oh, my God, Allison Jones, the greatest human ever, told me about this.

1360
01:00:10.890 --> 01:00:14.050
And they said, you're going in for the role of Dwight.

1361
01:00:14.150 --> 01:00:16.170
And I had been a huge fan of the British show.

1362
01:00:16.270 --> 01:00:18.450
And I was like, I don't know, man.

1363
01:00:18.530 --> 01:00:21.350
That's not, I don't know if I'm right for that role.

1364
01:00:21.370 --> 01:00:25.110
And so, I weirdly have no idea what I was thinking.

1365
01:00:25.110 --> 01:00:29.690
I said, you know what, I read the pilot and I said, you know what, I'm going to put my

1366
01:00:29.690 --> 01:00:30.370
best foot forward.

1367
01:00:30.550 --> 01:00:32.170
Let me know when they're casting Jim's.

1368
01:00:32.350 --> 01:00:36.670
And I remember the response from the NBC casting director to my manager at the time was,

1369
01:00:37.050 --> 01:00:39.370
no, but honestly, who does he think he is?

1370
01:00:39.670 --> 01:00:42.570
Like passing up an audition, an opportunity to audition.

1371
01:00:42.810 --> 01:00:44.810
And lo and behold, I thought it was over.

1372
01:00:44.950 --> 01:00:49.730
And I think it was like five, six weeks later that they called and they were like, all right,

1373
01:00:49.790 --> 01:00:51.930
they're looking for Jim's now and they'll have you back.

1374
01:00:53.070 --> 01:00:55.250
And then, oh my gosh, and that's so crazy.

1375
01:00:55.510 --> 01:01:00.570
And then when we finally did our screen test, you, you were living in New York and you had

1376
