to fly to LA for that screen teSt.

1377
01:01:04.670 --> 01:01:08.350
With all these New Yorkers that were auditioning, which was so much fun.

1378
01:01:08.350 --> 01:01:13.410
I remember I took the plane with Jim Gaffigan, who was auditioning for a role and it was like

1379
01:01:13.410 --> 01:01:13.990
laughing.

1380
01:01:14.390 --> 01:01:22.290
I mean, just was surrounded by heroes on the plane and then got to, um, got to the callback

1381
01:01:22.290 --> 01:01:23.910
or the test or whatever they called it.

1382
01:01:24.050 --> 01:01:26.390
And, um, cause I'm so, so experienced now.

1383
01:01:26.530 --> 01:01:31.190
I have no idea what I'm talking about, but, um, I remember getting in this big room and

1384
01:01:31.190 --> 01:01:34.090
it was the waiting room of where we actually shot our pilot.

1385
01:01:34.210 --> 01:01:39.170
I'm sure you guys have covered that, but like where we shot our pilot is what they measured

1386
01:01:39.170 --> 01:01:43.890
down to the quarter inch or centimeter to make our set, this building that existed.

1387
01:01:43.950 --> 01:01:44.990
We took an existing building.

1388
01:01:45.090 --> 01:01:51.230
And I remember sitting basically where like Ryan's desk, no, like where Mindy's desk was

1389
01:01:51.230 --> 01:01:56.390
like Toby and Mindy's desk was, I was sitting against that wall and I saw all these other

1390
01:01:56.390 --> 01:01:57.070
people coming in.

